<<<
6. Non-parallel ¢.-clauses in combination. Parallel ¢.-clauses can be strung together ad libitum, & may be rhetorically effective. It is otherwise with interdependent or dissimilar ¢.-clauses; for the principle see REPETITION.
===
**6.** Non-parallel *t.*-clauses in combination. Parallel *t.*-clauses can be strung together *ad libitum,* & may be rhetorically effective. It is otherwise with interdependent or dissimilar *t.*-clauses; for the principle see ^^REPETITION^^.
>>>

